From 1b0ca9c81c1fb000f88c02d0b9405d2337e11b69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:33:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: add RISCV64 support to GdbJIT

GdbJIT emits a tiny in-memory ELF object for the debugger to pick up.
Its DWARF unwinding register mapping hard-codes X86_64 and ARM64 and
falls through to the ARMv7 numbering for anything else, which is wrong
on RISCV64.

Add the missing CPU(RISCV64) branch: RegisterFP = 8 (s0/x8) and
RegisterLR = 1 (ra/x1), matching the RISC-V psABI's DWARF register
numbering.

This is a debug-only path; it has no effect on generated JIT code,
it just makes GdbJIT.cpp correct on RISCV64.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/GdbJIT.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/GdbJIT.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/GdbJIT.cpp
@@ -1164,6 +1164,11 @@ private:
 #elif CPU(ARM64)
         RegisterFP = 29,
         RegisterLR = 30,
+#elif CPU(RISCV64)
+        // RISC-V psABI: DWARF register numbers match x0..x31, so the frame
+        // pointer s0/x8 is 8 and the return-address register ra/x1 is 1.
+        RegisterFP = 8,
+        RegisterLR = 1,
 #else
         RegisterFP = 7,
         RegisterLR = 14,
